# Git and commit preferences

Keep in sync with `docs/git-commit-preferences.md`. Portfolio repo only — sibling tool remotes differ.

## Branching

- Never develop on `master`.
- Feature branches: `feature/<user>/<target-merge-branch>/<feature-name>` (user often `als`).
- Default integration: **`development`** (based on `master`).
- Merge features → `development` **without feature PRs**.
- When peers land on `development`, rebase/pull that tip onto the feature branch.
- When stable: merge `development` → `master` (user-guided); then FF `development` to that master tip.
- PRs mainly for `development` → `master`, guided by the user.
- Do not modify `master` unless the user explicitly asks.
- Always create a **local** branch so it shows in GitKraken (not remote-only).
- Same-VM: `git worktree add`, not shared checkout in place.

## Commits / landing

- Clear, focused commits; match recent `git log` on `development`.
- Local-first: prefer Austen’s machine checkout; after pushing `development`, sync his local checked-out `development`.
- Do not open unnecessary feature PRs when prefs say merge to `development` directly.

## PR text (when needed)

Concrete, plain prose. No jargon padding; Project banned-prose list applies to PR bodies.

## Sibling tools (not this repo)

Helper remotes often use `master` and may land without review. Confirm with `git ls-remote`. Those prefs are **not** for this portfolio repo.
